<TSL-SYSTEM Tools> %Music@music, A point-song module of TSL-SYSTEM.
Usage: COMMAND [ARGUMENT]

Crawl the public music library on the internet, download the selected
music to the local tools/Music/Musics directory, add it to the point-song
list, and control the background playback of the terminal.

Commands:
    search KEYWORD,     Crawl the internet and list the matched music.
    get INDEX/KEYWORD,  Download the selected music to the local
                        tools/Music/Musics directory and add it to the
                        point-song list.
    info INDEX/KEYWORD, Show the detailed information of a music.
    list,               List all the local music.
    local KEYWORD,      Search the local music by title, artist, album or
                        file name.
    queue,              Show the current point-song list.
    drop INDEX,         Remove the music at INDEX from the point-song list.
    clear,              Clear the point-song list.
    dir,                Show the music directory (tools/Music/Musics).
    play [INDEX/KEYWORD], Start or resume the background playback.
    pause,              Pause the background playback, or resume it if paused.
    stop,               Stop the background playback.

Identifies:
    @help,              Print this HelpPage.
    @exit,              Return to the Terminal.
    @flush,             Flush the temp of Music Module.

The index of the result of 'search' can be used by 'get' and 'info'; the
index of 'list' and 'local' can be used by 'play'. The crawler supports the
netease and kugou sources, and some music may be copyright restricted.
The playback state is shared, so 'pause' and 'stop' also work on the music
started by another terminal window.
